       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. That is typically 800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. The requested daily total is twice that limit, and the single dose is twice the usual maximum.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n2. **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia or antipyresis.\n3. **Ibuprofen 1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. The \"1600\" may have been meant as a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I can add that to the order note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
